title: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Result › Result first: eligibility, benefits, what the service needs
route: /authorizations/eligibility/R-1042
intro: How the three parts of the summary are worked out from the patient's row and from the saved Payers configuration. Eligibility says eligible, not eligible or needs a fix, with the dates. Benefits says covered or not, with the service limit and, only when the plan has them, copay, deductible and coinsurance. What this service needs says whether an authorization is required, on file or not required, and shows the payer's saved rules, read only.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: effective dates, limits and cost share are sample data, and the check is simulated.
---
start s1 "Result page, summary card"

group gE "Eligibility"
  decision e0 "What did the state or plan say?"
  process e1 "Pill 'Eligible' (green)\n'Effective 01/01/2026, no end date'"
  process e2 "Pill 'Not eligible' (red)\n'Effective 01/01/2026, ended 09/30/2026'"
  process e3 "Pill 'Needs a fix' (red)\n'Effective 01/01/2026, lapsed 10/12/2026'\nButton 'Request retro-eligibility'"
  process e4 "Pill 'Needs a fix' (red)\n'No coverage was found for these details. Check the member ID and date of birth, or read the card again.'\nNo dates"
endgroup

process nf "Benefits and What this service needs say 'Not checked' (grey)\n'Needs a plan that knows this member'\nNo limit line, no cost share, no Payers rules"

group gB "Benefits"
  decision b0 "What do the benefits say?"
  process b1 "Pill 'Covered' (green)\n'Residential 3.5 is payable. Codes H0018 and H0019'"
  process b2 "Pill 'Limited' (amber)\n'... is payable with conditions. Codes ...'"
  process b3 "Pill 'Not covered' (red)\n'... is not a covered benefit. Codes ...'"
  decision b4 "Is a service limit on file?"
  process b5 "Quiet line '9 of 14 days used, 5 left'\n(or '38 of 48 units used, 10 left')\n'All 14 days used. Nothing left' when none is left"
  process b6 "Quiet line 'No annual day limit for residential 3.5. The authorization sets the days'\nwhen the program has none (Summit residential)\nOtherwise no limit line"
  decision b7 "Does this plan type have a cost share on file?"
  process b8 "Quiet line 'Patient pays: Copay $40 per day, deductible $350 left, coinsurance 20% after the deductible'\nCommercial plans and carve-outs\nMedicare Advantage: 'Deductible $85 left, coinsurance 20%'"
  process b9 "Nothing about cost\nOhio Medicaid members usually pay none, so there is no '$0' line"
endgroup

group gN "What this service needs"
  decision n0 "What is the authorization state?"
  process n1 "Pill 'Not required' (grey)\n'Beacon does not require one for IOP.'"
  process n2 "Pill 'On file' (green)\n'On file with Summit.'"
  process n3 "Pill 'Required, not on file' (amber)\n'Required before the first day. Not on file yet.'"
  process n4 "Pills 'In progress', 'Payer reviewing' or 'Retro request open' (amber or grey)\nwith what is happening to the request"
  process n5 "Quiet line from the Payers config, read live\n'Summit's saved rules (demo data): Notice within 24 hours of admission.\n9 documents on the Residential 3.5 list.'\nEdit the rule or the list on Payers and this line follows"
  click n6 "Click 'Open Summit's rules'"
endgroup

process note "Under the summary: 'Active coverage does not mean this service is covered.\nCheck the benefits and the authorization requirement.'"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › Rules › Read the rules"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Result › Next actions"
goto g3 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Result › Which verdict and why"

s1 --> e0
e0 -->|Active| e1 --> b0
e0 -->|Ended| e2 --> b0
e0 -->|Lapsed| e3 --> b0
e0 -->|Not found| e4 --> nf --> note
b0 -->|Covered| b1 --> b4
b0 -->|Limited| b2 --> b4
b0 -->|Not covered| b3 --> b4
b4 -->|Yes| b5 --> b7
b4 -->|No| b6 --> b7
b7 -->|Yes| b8 --> n0
b7 -->|No| b9 --> n0
n0 -->|Not required| n1 --> n5
n0 -->|On file| n2 --> n5
n0 -->|Required| n3 --> n5
n0 -->|Drafted, reviewing, retro| n4 --> n5
n5 --> n6 --> g1
n5 --> note --> g3
e3 -.-> g2
